WEBVTT

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.540
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.790
Here we are.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.710
It's the last day.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:55.210
We just need to do 
what we always do.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.720
<b>Last Day</b>

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.720
<b>Free Entry</b>

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.720
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium</b>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.800
All these people...

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.280
I'm glad they came, 
but they could have come earlier.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.060
Jeez.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.450
Director!

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:14.650
It's been a while.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.150
You came.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.530
You raised us, Director.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.160
You were more work than the fish.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.080
Long time, Master!

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.060
Hey.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.500
I haven't seen you in a while.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.430
We wanted to congratulate you 
on your work.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:32.540
Thanks for coming all this way.

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:37.990
Looks like people are here 
from aquariums all around.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.000
Why would they bother?

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.310
I told you.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.560
The director was known 
as the legendary aquarium keeper.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.830
Then I wish they'd have come sooner 
and helped Gama Gama.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:53.200
Everyone's busy working with
the creatures at other aquariums.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.300
The director wouldn't let them 
set their work aside to come see him.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.190
That's true.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:03.960
But they came from
far away just for today.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:07.450
I'm proud to be part of Gama Gama, too.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:09.690
That's true.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.470
Hey.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.920
Welcome.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.600
We came to visit.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.050
Is this a message area?

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.410
Yeah.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.470
I thought I'd get people 
to write their goodbyes to Gama Gama.

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.770
I want to write one, too!

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.760
Oh, yeah, I have a message 
from Airi-chan in the hospital, too.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.310
<b>I love Gama Gama!

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.500
May I put it up with the others?

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.570
Of course!

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.570
<b>I had my first date with my husband 
at this aquarium. Thank you 
for being open all these years.</b>

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:50.080
Fuuka-chan!

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.270
Maho-chan!

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:58.250
Since this is the last time,
may I request something?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.130
You gonna quiz me again?

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.130
Can we get a picture together please?

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.410
I won't forget Gama Gama!

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:26.040
Kukuru, this is Hoshino-san, 
the director from Aquarium Tingaara.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.490
Oh, hi.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.890
Kukuru-san!

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:30.480
Nice to meet you.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.680
You're still a student, and you managed 
to serve as acting director, huh?

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.080
I'm amazed.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.040
You have management talent.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.300
No, I kept messing up.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:46.930
Tingaara is going to be looking 
after a lot of our critters.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.760
Including you, Kukuru.

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:53.850
They say they'd love to have you, 
if you'd like.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:05:02.520
We're more than happy to welcome anyone 
who knows a lot about aquariums.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.210
Wait...

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.470
You haven't decided what you're going to do 
after school, have you?

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:06.890
H-Hold on!

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.820
This is too soon.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.950
Did we surprise you?

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.840
You don't need to hurry to answer.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.750
Give it plenty of thought.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:18.740
Okay.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.970
Thank you.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.990
Thank you.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.010
Take care!

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.780
It's over, huh?

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.580
Thanks, everyone.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.810
We'll have a little party later.

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:02.250
We can clean up tomorrow.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.500
Okay.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.960
Good work.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.900
Cheers!

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.620
Well, eat up!

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.360
Thanks, Udon-chan!

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.330
You two worked so hard.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.100
Good job!

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.760
To be honest, 
I didn't do good enough.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.070
Sorry for getting you all involved.

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:26.780
Oh, stop it.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.070
Just drink.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.780
Why are you the one 
drinking so much?

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.740
Shut your yakking, Yakamashi.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:38.000
Thanks for helping so much, everyone.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.620
You, too, Kai. Thanks.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.750
It's fine. I had fun.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:45.210
Also, Kukuru, 
what are you going to do now?

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.220
Umi-yan and Kuuya-san are going 
to Tingaara, aren't they?

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.220
Oh, yeah.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:55.680
Actually, they asked me if I want to come 
after I graduate from high school.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.860
To Tingaara?

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:58.810
Huh.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.610
You have a job lined up, then!

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:03.580
I'd never even thought about it.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.440
I don't know yet.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:09.400
It sounds good to me.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:10.960
She's right.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.950
You'd be wasting a career
opportunity, Kukuru.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:14.620
Yeah.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:19.000
I'm just going to say it:

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.770
I want to quit my job
 and work at Tingaara!

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:25.290
Wait, what? 
What are you talking about?

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.510
I don't know if I'll
be accepted yet, though.

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:32.840
Remember I told you that I wanted 
to work at an aquarium when I was a kid?

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.680
Yeah.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:38.880
I remembered how much I loved it, 
when I helped with the traveling aquarium.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:44.560
I saw how you didn't give up, and you gave
me the confidence to give it a shot, Kukuru.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:45.690
Thank you!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.070
I can't breathe, Karin-chan!

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.630
Does that mean you might
be working together with Kukuru?

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.120
Lucky.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.410
Maybe I'll find work around there, too.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:57.450
What about Kamee?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:02.030
I want to try studying
cooking properly sometime.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:04.540
It'll be lonely if you all go.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.880
When are you leaving, Fuuka-chan?

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.240
I'm planning to get on
the plane tomorrow.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.170
School starts right after.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:15.590
The month went by so quickly!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.930
I'm going to miss you!

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:24.570
Finally, let's have a word 
from the director.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:28.540
Here.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.700
Good work, everyone.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:41.290
I feel very fortunate to have had 
so many people stay until the very end.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:45.920
I enjoy seeing kids come to Gama Gama.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:50.300
When they're looking at the sea creatures, 
their eyes light up.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:53.600
Some children are changed just a little bit, 
starting the next day.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.690
They might finish their whole plate of fish,

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:58.160
or they might take some litter home 
from the beach.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:02.310
When you come to love living things, 
you become a kinder person.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:06.250
I want everyone 
to continue loving living things,

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:08.410
and I want any of you 
who work at an aquarium

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:11.820
to continue being the kindest people of all.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:16.510
Gama Gama may be closing, 
but you aren't done yet.

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:20.830
I'll read my favorite poem 
for those of you who are leaving.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:27.190
"Endless Oceans," by Kudo Naoko-san.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:34.460
"The briny ocean born of the human spirit 
is endless, always overflowing..."

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:41.990
Hey, Fuuka...

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:45.760
Can I say something 
that isn't really my business?

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:46.520
Sure.

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:49.440
Why don't you go ahead 
with that movie?

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:52.780
If you still have a chance 
to go after your dream,

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.980
you should fight for it until the end.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.320
What about you?

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.740
Are you still not sure about Tingaara?

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.830
We don't need to talk about me.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:05.790
Yes, we do!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:10.010
You haven't smiled at all 
since the typhoon.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:11.390
I have!

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:12.260
See?

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.700
It's too dark to see.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.080
This is my request of a lifetime.

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:23.120
Please go after your dream again, Fuuka.

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:24.310
For my sake, too.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:26.580
For your sake?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:27.350
Yeah.

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:32.200
My dream's finished, 
but I think if I see you striving for yours,

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:34.600
I can stay strong, too.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:38.900
I'm going to support your dream this time.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.600
<i>If that'll make you smile.</i>

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:53.420
I have a flight to Tokyo 
booked for tomorrow.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.280
I'll go accept the movie deal.

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:56.920
<b>Our Oceans are Endless</b>

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:03.370
Do what's right, 
and everything will work out.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.760
I'll be home in time 
for when you leave.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:09.620
Okay.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.320
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium is closing</b>

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.320
<b>Thank you for 48 years of patronage</b>

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:28.170
There we go.

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.000
What are we doing with these fish?

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:36.090
Some of them will be going 
to the aquariums that wanted them.

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:40.160
Most of the rest will
be going to Tingaara.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:43.020
The director said he would take care 
of them until they move.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.990
Help me carry these.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.170
Okay.

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:52.810
How do you get hired 
as an employee at an aquarium?

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:54.080
Dunno.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.660
I guess it depends.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:58.020
It's probably easier 
if you have work experience.

00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.550
Why?

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:01.280
No, just wondering.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:02.750
Hang on!

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.700
Let me check off the list.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:15.690
You can leave behind anything 
you don't need.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:18.490
Those boots are going to be a pain 
to carry, aren't they?

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:20.890
Nah, I'll take them home.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:30.160
Thank you for letting me stay 
for such a long time.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:32.010
Not at all.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:34.060
Meet once, and we're siblings, right?

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.360
I'm glad you came, too.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:41.190
I bet this is what it would have
been like if Kukuru had siblings.

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:44.300
Kukuru said the same thing.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:48.650
She says she imagines 
having an older sister.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.830
Lunch time, Choko.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:58.330
Sorry!

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:00.040
Hold still.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.510
Thanks for taking them.

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:05.670
See you later.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.200
Sad, isn't it?

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.050
Yeah.

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:15.440
<b>Sold out!</b>

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.440
<b>Goodbye, Gama Gama</b>

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.450
<b>Thank you, Gama Gama!!</b>

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.450
<b>The sea snakes 
were awesome</b>

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.450
<b>Thank you 
for letting me see the fish
Nakamura Hiyori</b>

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.450
<b>Gama Gama forever!!</b>

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:27.450
<b>To everyone at Gama Gama Aquarium
Thank you for the past 48 years.
I've come many times to treat the animals. 
The kids here are always so full of life. 
I could tell they were taken really good care of.
Gama Gama is a special place to me.
The miracle I saw that day will stay with me forever.
I'm sad to see it go, but I'm determined to take 
what I learned here and continue working with 
animals going forward. I hope to work 
with all of you somewhere, someday.
Thank you very much.
Takeshita</b>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
<b>I love Gama Gama!</b>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
<b>The frogfish are
 so cute it hurts.</b>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
<b>Thanks for the heals <3</b>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
<b>I love penguins</b>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
<b>Thank you</b>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
<b>Gama Gama Aquarium,
Thank you for the past 48 years
Our family has many memories here.</b>

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.450
<b>I had my first date with my husband 
at this aquarium. Thank you 
for being open all these years.</b>

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:31.990
Thank you, too.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:14:00.550
<i>I never knew it's so lonely 
without the animals.</i>

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.560
What time should we leave?

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.240
We should get going.

00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:38.300
Sorry, I know you're busy.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.770
Nah, it's just cleanup that's left.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:44.730
I can't stand to watch 
Gama Gama get hollowed out.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:47.280
Thanks for giving me a
reason to go outside.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.730
Really?

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:49.400
Yeah.

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:52.280
Also, I saw a weird illusion.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.360
It was my doppelgänger!

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:55.410
Say what?

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.070
My lookalike.

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:58.510
She was like my twin.

00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:01.770
She seemed kind of nice, though.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:03.340
She was smiling.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:08.160
That might be your big sister, Kukuru.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:15.180
Maybe she came to see you just once 
before Gama Gama goes away.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.400
What are you talking about?

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:30.070
We were going to tell you 
once you grew up.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:26.940
<b>Maternity Handbook</b>

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:26.940
<b>Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:34.420
You had a twin sister, Kukuru.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:39.960
But you were the only one born.

00:15:40.800 --> 00:15:43.320
We don't know why.

00:15:43.320 --> 00:15:47.420
But having twin girls is hard.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:50.800
You must know from your time 
at Gama Gama.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.640
Life is difficult.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.740
That's why living things are precious.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:16:02.720
She must have been watching over
Gama Gama all this time, too.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.280
The illusion I saw today...

00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.840
It wasn't the first time.

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:25.380
I wonder if she was there 
all this time.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:31.880
I wonder if I'm not going 
to see her once Gama Gama's gone.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.060
Kukuru.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:47.020
I need to get going.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.660
Oh, right.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:50.280
Are you all right?

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.680
Sorry for worrying you.

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.000
Don't say that.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.820
I'm so bad.

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:59.410
You're about to set out for your dream.

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:02.830
Off you go.

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:05.370
Yeah. I'll be going.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:08.840
Thanks for everything, Kukuru.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:11.920
Make your dream happen, Fuuka.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:37.260
<i>I know what happens.</i>

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:43.130
<i>When someone loses their dreams, it's only
once they're alone that they can really cry.</i>

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:53.130
<i>JFA Flight 917 for Tokyo is now 
welcoming all passengers aboard.</i>

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:57.560
<i>Please board at Gate 24.</i>

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.900
<i>She must be crying about now.</i>

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:03.680
<i>I can't!</i>

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.190
Hi, I'm sorry!

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.360
<i>I can't leave her.</i>

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:20.460
<i>Kukuru doesn't know 
how much she saved me.</i>

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:25.520
<b>Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.000
<b>Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.070
Hello?

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:31.400
<i>Fuuka?</i>

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:33.000
Where are you right now?!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.900
Kukuru!

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:46.390
Fuuka?

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:48.670
Why?

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:49.720
What about your flight?

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:51.020
I don't care!

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:53.900
You're more important to me right now.

00:18:57.170 --> 00:19:01.150
You gave me so much strength 
at Gama Gama.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:03.410
I can finally smile now.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.140
So I can't leave you when you're crying!

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.040
You aren't alone anymore.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:12.670
I'm going to be your big sister.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.110
I booked a flight and a night bus.

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:34.960
I'll have to make a connection, 
but I'll make it home by morning.

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.910
Iwate's far, huh?

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.000
It's close.

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.540
I'll be back to see you soon.

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:41.320
What about your movie?

00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:47.210
I'm relieved, now that I finally know 
how I really feel.

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:51.830
My dream had ended when I came here.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:54.180
Oh.

00:19:55.150 --> 00:20:00.190
Kukuru, will you cheer me on 
when I find a new dream?

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.090
Of course.

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:05.760
I think I'll go to Tingaara.

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:12.250
I asked you to chase after your dream 
for my sake again, remember?

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:13.350
Yeah.

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:16.090
I wonder if you feel the same way.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:19.320
If I stay strong, you can, too.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.860
If I'm crying, 
you'll come back worried.

00:20:23.250 --> 00:20:24.480
Sorry.

00:20:24.480 --> 00:20:25.570
It was an impulsive thing.

00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:28.640
I want you to come back with a smile.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.760
That means I have to smile first.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:35.580
I have a better chance 
if I'm at an aquarium, right?

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:39.160
I'll do my best away from Gama Gama.

00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:44.010
I don't want to forget 
that being alive isn't a given.

00:20:44.550 --> 00:20:47.300
I want the people watching me 
to be proud of me.

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:49.630
I'm going to work hard.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:51.060
For her sake, too.

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:59.820
<b>Sorry for the late reply.
Thank you for inviting me 
to work on the movie.
Unfortunately, I will have 
to decline the offer.</b>

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:13.500
<i>"Endless Oceans."</i>

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:20.250
<i>"The briny ocean born of the human spirit 
is endless, always overflowing."</i>

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:26.260
<i>"The ocean mixes everything together, 
and the ocean remains the ocean."</i>

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:30.120
<i>"Splashes of happiness melt away 
and become the ocean."</i>

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:34.020
<i>"Lumps of sadness melt away 
and become the ocean."</i>

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:41.770
<i>"Surprise, fear, shame, pride... 
All things melt and become the ocean."</i>

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:48.780
<i>"When a person peers into the ocean within, 
strangely, they find peace."</i>

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:51.780
<i>"They find peace, 
and they think to themselves:</i>

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.740
<i>'See you tomorrow.'"</i>
